<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Qapu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ali Qapu is a palace on the western side of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naqsh-e-jahan-square">Naqsh-e Jahan Square</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, built under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> around the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Abbas I</a>. It served as a grand gateway and reception palace, with an elevated veranda from which the shah viewed events in the square. It is a celebrated example of Safavid architecture and decoration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-qapu.jpg" alt="Ali Qapu" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amir Pashaei · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C4%80l%C4%AB_Q%C4%81p%C5%AB_in_golden_time.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
